{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":182478,"name":"jim jones","username":"jim_jones","avatar_template":"/letter_avatar/jim_jones/{size}/5_5575768a8748004e209b776fc1b2916d.png","created_at":"2019-06-05T18:38:47.685Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI have one of these devices lying and am looking for any help on getting openwrt on it.\u003cbr\u003e\nI've googled it but can't find much help on building an image for it.\u003cbr\u003e\nI don't care about the VDSL/ADSL modem in it, and I know its not supported.\u003cbr\u003e\nSo can anyone give me any hints on if its possible and/or how to build an image for this device?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks Jim\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2019-06-05T19:09:44.936Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":852,"reads":26,"readers_count":25,"score":4265.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":38313,"topic_slug":"adding-openwrt-support-for-zyxel-sbg3300-n","display_username":"jim jones","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":3,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":15596,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/adding-openwrt-support-for-zyxel-sbg3300-n/38313/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":182497,"name":"Jeff","username":"jeff","avatar_template":"/letter_avatar/jeff/{size}/5_5575768a8748004e209b776fc1b2916d.png","created_at":"2019-06-05T19:37:43.264Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThe \"firehose\" is \u003ca href=\"https://openwrt.org/docs/guide-developer/adding_new_device\"\u003ehttps://openwrt.org/docs/guide-developer/adding_new_device\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNot much on \u003ca href=\"https://wikidevi.com/wiki/ZyXEL\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ehttps://wikidevi.com/wiki/ZyXEL\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://wikidevi.com/w/index.php?title=ZyXEL_SBG3300-N\u0026amp;action=edit\u0026amp;redlink=1\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eZyXEL SBG3300-N\u003c/a\u003e Series -  \u003cem\u003eWireless N VDSL2 Combo WAN Small Business Security Gateway\u003c/em\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cem\u003eZyXEL SBG3300-N\u003c/em\u003e  - \u003ca href=\"https://wikidevi.com/wiki/Broadcom\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eBroadcom\u003c/a\u003e BCM6368 chipset (G.INP)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNot a chip I know off the top of my head, but Broadcom \u003cem\u003ewireless\u003c/em\u003e is always a problem as it effectively doesn't support open-source projects. (Broadcom \"CPUs\" are not always so much of an issue.)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSeveral devices in varying states of OpenWrt support listed at \u003ca href=\"https://openwrt.org/toh/views/toh_extended_all?dataflt%5BCPU*~%5D=BCM6368\"\u003ehttps://openwrt.org/toh/views/toh_extended_all?dataflt[CPU*~]=BCM6368\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMost of them look to have a 400 MHz MIPS core, which is pretty underpowered these days. The 750 MHz class, MIPS-based processors in \"last-generation\", all-in-one routers can barely handle a couple hundred Mbps, so this SoC is probably half of that (even though dual-core), though in keeping with its 100 Mbps Ethernet.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI would find it hard to justify the time myself, given that one can now buy a good-quality all-in-one starting at US$20 or so. It might be an interesting \"project\", but if that's what you're after, I'd recommend a more current, perhaps better documented device.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2019-06-05T19:38:09.097Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":25,"reads":24,"readers_count":23,"score":134.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":38313,"topic_slug":"adding-openwrt-support-for-zyxel-sbg3300-n","display_username":"Jeff","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://openwrt.org/toh/views/toh_extended_all?dataflt%5BCPU*~%5D=BCM6368","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"OpenWrt Project: Table of Hardware: Full details","clicks":36},{"url":"https://openwrt.org/docs/guide-developer/adding_new_device","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"OpenWrt Project: Adding a new device","clicks":31},{"url":"https://wikidevi.com/wiki/ZyXEL","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"ZyXEL - WikiDevi","clicks":22},{"url":"https://wikidevi.com/w/index.php?title=ZyXEL_SBG3300-N\u0026action=edit\u0026redlink=1","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Creating ZyXEL SBG3300-N - WikiDevi","clicks":21},{"url":"https://wikidevi.com/wiki/Broadcom","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Broadcom - WikiDevi","clicks":2}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":2354,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/adding-openwrt-support-for-zyxel-sbg3300-n/38313/2","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":fa